chord-ocr.onnx, chord-ocr-hand.onnx — chord-symbol recognisers for the "Scan 📷" mode (a photo or scanned
PDF of a lead sheet → chord chart). Input: [1, 1, 32, W] — one box of text, 32 px tall, ink = 1, paper = 0
(engine.tsx chordOcrInput). Output: logits [1, W/4, 43] — CTC over the chord as drawn ("ABCDEFG",
"abdgijlmnostuM", digits, "#/()+-,Δ°ø^"; class 0 = blank). The engine decodes it (ctcBeam), keeps the most
probable reading the chord grammar accepts (chordOcrRead / chordFromWritten) and reads bar numbers (chordOcrNumber).

Two readers, same network (the page picks one: "Book style"):
  chord-ocr.onnx       "printed" — the default. The first model (2026-11-10) fine-tuned 3,000 steps with 30 % of
                       the images in the hand-copied Real Book style (scripts/chord-ocr/synth_rb.py); it passed
                       every regression check on engraved, photographed and held-out-handwriting text.
  chord-ocr-hand.onnx  "hand" — the same recipe with a finer pen in synth_rb.py, step 1,000. Reads hand-copied
                       Real Book pages best, but on engraved pages it can take a bar number for a letter and it
                       is ~2 points lower on the held-out handwriting fonts. Measurements: docs/OMR-PLAN.md.
Model:          our own — a CNN (6 conv layers, 32→128 channels) + a bidirectional GRU (96 per side) + a
                linear layer, 588,011 parameters, weight-only int8 (per-output-row scale + DequantizeLinear;
                activations fp32). Written and trained for this project; no third-party weights.
Licence:        MIT, as the rest of this repository (see LICENSE).
Training data:  synthetic only. Chord symbols sampled from fake-book spellings (maj7 / MA7 / Δ7 / M7, mi7 / -7,
                ø, °, +, sus, 69, parenthesised alterations, slash basses), bar numbers (labelled with their
                digits) and non-chord text (section names, tempo marks, directions, lyric words — labelled
                empty), drawn with 25 open-licensed fonts (SIL OFL 1.1; Permanent Marker, Coming Soon and
                Schoolbell: Apache 2.0) plus system DejaVu / FreeFont / Liberation Sans, ♯ ♭ from music-capable
                fonts or typed as # b, raised/smaller suffixes, italics, then rotation, blur, low resolution,
                noise, paper tone, stray staff lines and JPEG. No font is distributed with the app.
                Held out (never trained on): Liberation Serif, Kalam, Schoolbell.
How it was made: scripts/chord-ocr/ — fetch_fonts.sh, synth.py, train.py (CTC, AdamW, one-cycle), export.py
                (ONNX opset 17, checked against PyTorch, then the int8 step); the fine-tunes: from_onnx.py (the
                first model's weights recovered from its ONNX), synth_rb.py, finetune.py. The hand-copied images
                also use MuseJazz Text (© 2016 Torsten Hämmerle, Abraham Lee; SIL OFL 1.1). README.md there has
                the commands and the measurements.
